  "assessment": "Reviewed all twelve direct interests, thirty-three supporting topics, six illustrations and twelve outcomes. Learning, teaching, social context and evidence-informed improvement anchor the closest option. Technology and learning-environment design support a cognitive and computational direction with explicit limits on specialist instructional design. Lifelong learning supports a workplace direction, corroborated by the eighteen EC sequence in organisation and consultancy and the economics course. Illustrative VR, podcast and museum examples and graduate outcomes do not create standalone pathways.",
